{
  "type": "",
  "$comment": "Elicitation is the schema's densest nesting: a request is a union of modes and each mode is a union of scopes in the same JSON object, and both of the schema's maps whose values are a union live here. The map cases are the layer-1 evidence for a codec that used to drop the discriminant those values are chosen by.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a form elicitation scoped to a session",
      "type": "CreateElicitationRequest",
      "why": "the common shape: a mode and a scope flattened into the object the message already is",
      "input": {
        "message": "which branch?",
        "mode": "form",
        "requestedSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "branch": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "sessionId": "sess-1"
      },
      "accepted": true,
      "normalized": {
        "sessionId": "sess-1",
        "requestedSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "branch": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "mode": "form",
        "message": "which branch?"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a form elicitation tied to a tool call",
      "type": "CreateElicitationRequest",
      "why": "the session scope's optional toolCallId, which an agent relaying an MCP server's elicitation sets",
      "input": {
        "message": "which branch?",
        "mode": "form",
        "requestedSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {}
        },
        "sessionId": "sess-1",
        "toolCallId": "call-1"
      },
      "accepted": true,
      "normalized": {
        "sessionId": "sess-1",
        "toolCallId": "call-1",
        "requestedSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {}
        },
        "mode": "form",
        "message": "which branch?"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a form elicitation scoped to a request",
